\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. When mothers of Salem,
\par Their children brought to Jesus,
\par The stern desciples drove them back
\par And bade them depart;
\par But Jesus saw them ere they fled,
\par And sweetly smiled, and kindly said:
\par Suffer the children to come unto Me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. How kind was our Saviour
\par To bid those children welcome;
\par But there are many thousands
\par Who have never heard His name;
\par Dear Saviour, hear us when we pray,
\par That they may hear Thee to them say:
\par Suffer the children to come unto Me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. And soon may the heathen
\par Of every tribe and nation
\par Fulfil Thy blessed word, and cast 
\par Their idols all away;
\par O shine upon them from above,
\par And show Thyself a God of love;
\par Teach them, dear Saviour, to come unto Thee.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

